est.raises(ValueError, match=\"design_authoring_batch\"):\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-game-identity.md:13:| GAME-005 | Trustworthy return play | Local progress, save/resume, approved offline content, settings, and recovery support safe return. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GC0001.md:4:dependencies: G0001,G0002,G0003,G0004,G0005\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GC0001.md:6:source_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GAME-005,GAME-006,GAME-007,GAME-008,GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007,GPI-008,GPI-009,GPI-010,GPI-011,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:39:### Round, score, and progress rules \u2014 `GAME-005` to `GAME-008`\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:48:| GAME-005 | **Round \u201cFirst Whistle.\u201d** Tutorial round contains 5 fixed, original tutorial cards (`TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05`) covering selecting, typing, feedback, explanation, and pause/save. It is intentionally non-timed. | This is the complete first useful journey. Completion creates/updates local milestone `first_whistle_complete`; it cannot require account, network, purchase, or deferred content. Test: a new local profile can complete it offline and resume after app restart. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:49:| GAME-006 | **Round \u201cMixed Fixture.\u201d** A 10-card themed round draws from one selected category or the Kickoff Mix, with no more than two adjacent cards sharing format or difficulty. The player may pause; a displayed timer mode is optional and defaults off. | First release ships one tutorial and one configurable standard round template, no ranked/daily/live/event modes. Test: deterministic seed produces ten eligible cards and valid format alternation or records the shortage. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:50:| GAME-007 | **Scoring and streak.** Correct = 100 points; a consecutive-correct streak of 3+ adds 25 points to each later correct answer, capped at +100. Incorrect, timeout (only if enabled), blank submission, or abandon resets the active streak; score never decreases. Explanation is available after resolution. | No paid boosts, leaderboard, social comparison, or opaque difficulty multiplier. Test: table-driven sequence proves cap, reset, and per-attempt result; a retry is a new run, not an overwrite of history. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:51:| GAME-008 | **Result and return.** Results show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, and next action: replay, choose theme, or exit. Progress is local milestones and aggregate history only, not RPG levels. | An interrupted run persists at a safe boundary before the next unresolved question. Completed result is idempotent: reopening cannot award twice. Test: complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupted draft, and delete-history paths are specified. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:53:**Dependencies:** GAME-005 needs published tutorial cards and persistence;\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:54:GAME-006 needs GAME-001\u2013004; GAME-007 consumes adjudication events; GAME-008\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:94:| GAME-005\u2013008 | J1/J2/J3 | A shell/progress; C rules/score/feedback; D persistence for return |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:2:task_id: G0004\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:4:dependencies: G0003\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:6:source_catalogue_ids: GAME-007,GAME-008,GPI-010,GPI-011\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:10:design_authoring_batch: GB0002\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:15:Write accepted evidence for GAME-007\u2013008/GPI-010\u2013011: 100-point capped-streak table, feedback equivalents, result states, milestone idempotence, and 18 edge/lifecycle fixtures.\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:2:task_id: G0005\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:4:dependencies: GB0003,G0004\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:10:design_authoring_batch: GB0003\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/05-delivery-map.md:34:| DM-05 | Produce and validate TUT-01\u201305, GPI-008, as a fixed accessible offline tutorial package. | DM-03\u201304; accepted G evidence | `content/tutorial/`; tutorial fixtures | Every named card resolves and tutorial fixture completes once. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/05-delivery-map.md:45:| DM-11 | Implement First Whistle lifecycle and one-time local milestone from GPI-008. | DM-02, 05\u201306, 10 | `src/core/tutorial/`; `tests/core/tutorial.*` | Offline start, resolve, restart, and idempotent milestone tests. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/05-delivery-map.md:46:| DM-12 | Implement Mixed Fixture lifecycle and GPI-009 deterministic eligible 10-card selection. | DM-02, 04, 06, 10 | `src/core/round/`; `tests/core/round.*` | Seeded selection, optional timer, pause, shortage and safe-boundary tests. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/05-delivery-map.md:47:| DM-13 | Implement GPI-010 score/streak and GPI-011 result events with explainable feedback. | DM-06, 12 | `src/core/{score,results}`; fixtures | Cap/reset/blank/abandon/non-decreasing/idempotent-complete tests. |\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md:91:are created \u2192 resolved \u2192 summarised; streak resets per GAME-007. **Rules:**\n./projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json:6:    {\"id\": \"IMP-FT-001\", \"title\": \"Implement curated quiz content and round rules\", \"crea