progress-rules\",\n      \"production_kind\": \"systemic_rules\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GPI-010\",\n      \"game_design_id\": \"GAME-007\",\n      \"selected_module\": \"round-score-and-progress-rules\",\n      \"content_design_card_type\": \"score and feedback rule table\",\n      \"finite_item_or_catalogue_batch\": \"one 100-point base / capped 3+ streak rule table\",\n      \"planned_quantity\": \"1 rule table; 12 edge-case fixtures\",\n      \"original_brief\": \"Make momentum celebratory but recoverable: wrong, blank, timeout, and abandon reset streak without negative score.\",\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"GPI-006\",\n        \"GPI-009\"\n      ],\n      \"asset_ids\": [\n        \"ASSET-FBK-001\",\n        \"ASSET-FBK-002\",\n        \"ASSET-FBK-003\"\n      ],\n      \"audio_ids\": [\n        \"AUDIO-QZ-002\",\n        \"AUDIO-QZ-003\",\n        \"AUDIO-QZ-004\"\n      ],\n      \"implementation_outcome\": \"Accessible state events for score, streak, correction, and celebration.\",\n      \"owner\": \"Game rules designer + accessibility reviewer\",\n      \"verification\": \"Fixtures prove cap, reset, monotonic total, text/pattern equivalent, reduced-motion and muted outcomes.\",\n      \"module\": \"round-score-and-progress-rules\",\n      \"production_kind\": \"systemic_rules\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GPI-011\",\n      \"game_design_id\": \"GAME-008\",\n      \"selected_module\": \"round-score-and-progress-rules\",\n      \"content_design_card_type\": \"results and milestone surface\",\n      \"finite_item_or_catalogue_batch\": \"one result summary and first_whistle_complete milestone\",\n      \"planned_quantity\": \"2 named states; 6 lifecycle fixtures\",\n      \"original_brief\": \"Show score, streak outcome, next action, and learning-oriented explanation without rank, loot, or social comparison.\",\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"GPI-009\",\n        \"GPI-010\",\n        \"GPI-014\"\n      ],\n      \"asset_ids\": [\n        \"ASSET-FBK-004\",\n        \"ASSET-UI-001\"\n      ],\n      \"audio_ids\": [\n        \"AUDIO-RES-001\"\n      ],\n      \"implementation_outcome\": \"Idempotent completion state compatible with safe local resume.\",\n      \"owner\": \"Game designer + UI engineer\",\n      \"verification\": \"Complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupt draft, and deletion flows preserve one result/milestone.\",\n      \"module\": \"round-score-and-progress-rules\",\n      \"production_kind\": \"systemic_rules\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GPI-012\",\n      \"game_design_id\": \"GAME-009\",\n      \"selected_module\": \"accessible-recoverable-multitarget-experience\",\n      \"content_design_card_type\": \"guided-start and accessibility action map\",\n      \"finite_item_or_catalogue_batch\": \"local profile, tutorial entry, settings, 4 semantic input adapters\",\n      \"planned_quantity\": \"4 mappings: touch, pointer, keyboard, gamepad\",\n      \"original_brief\": \"Every action is labelled and equivalently available; focus, captions, contrast, text scaling, and reduced motion are designed in.\",\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"asset_ids\": [\n        \"ASSET-SHL-001\",\n        \"ASSET-UI-001\",\n        \"ASSET-UI-003\"\n      ],\n      \"audio_ids\": [\n        \"AUDIO-SET-001\"\n      ],\nequivalents for cues, and a reduced-motion feedback path are required. Original\ncue families: prompt arrival, correct, incorrect, streak rise, and saved state;\neach has a mute/volume path and no cue conveys information unavailable in text.\n\n### Round, score, and progress rules \u2014 `GAME-005` to `GAME-008`\n\n**Player outcome:** complete a clear, fair themed round and understand a local\nmilestone. **Entities:** `RoundDefinition`, `RoundRun`, `QuestionAttempt`,\n`AnswerSubmission`, `ScoreEvent`, `StreakState`, `TimerState`, `ResultSummary`,\n`LocalMilestone`, and `SelectionSeed`.\n\n| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GAME-005 | **Round \u201cFirst Whistle.\u201d** Tutorial round contains 5 fixed, original tutorial cards (`TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05`) covering selecting, typing, feedback, explanation, and pause/save. It is intentionally non-timed. | This is the complete first useful journey. Completion creates/updates local milestone `first_whistle_complete`; it cannot require account, network, purchase, or deferred content. Test: a new local profile can complete it offline and resume after app restart. |\n| GAME-006 | **Round \u201cMixed Fixture.\u201d** A 10-card themed round draws from one selected category or the Kickoff Mix, with no more than two adjacent cards sharing format or difficulty. The player may pause; a displayed timer mode is optional and defaults off. | First release ships one tutorial and one configurable standard round template, no ranked/daily/live/event modes. Test: deterministic seed produces ten eligible cards and valid format alternation or records the shortage. |\n| GAME-007 | **Scoring and streak.** Correct = 100 points; a consecutive-correct streak of 3+ adds 25 points to each later correct answer, capped at +100. Incorrect, timeout (only if enabled), blank submission, or abandon resets the active streak; score never decreases. Explanation is available after resolution. | No paid boosts, leaderboard, social comparison, or opaque difficulty multiplier. Test: table-driven sequence proves cap, reset, and per-attempt result; a retry is a new run, not an overwrite of history. |\n| GAME-008 | **Result and return.** Results show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, and next action: replay, choose theme, or exit. Progress is local milestones and aggregate history only, not RPG levels. | An interrupted run persists at a safe boundary before the next unresolved question. Completed result is idempotent: reopening cannot award twice. Test: complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupted draft, and delete-history paths are specified. |\n\n**Dependencies:** GAME-005 needs published tutorial cards and persistence;\nGAME-006 needs GAME-001\u2013004; GAME-007 consumes adjudication events; GAME-008\nconsumes score events and save/recovery. Visual family is bold category panels,\nneutral answer controls, and non-colour success/error indicators; audio is\nsupportive, optional, and captioned.\n\n### Accessible, recoverable multi-target experience \u2014 `GAME-009` to `GAME-012`\n\n**Player outcome:** start, control, interrupt, recover, and return to a round\nconfidently on a supported surface. **Entities:** `LocalProfile`, `Settings`,\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short\nrg -n --glob 'G*.md' '\"'^design_authoring_batch: GB0002$|''^task_id: G'\"' projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks\nsed -n '70,112p' supervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py\nsed -n '150,205p' README.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n M .env\n?? projects/final-fantasy/\n?? projects/football-trivia-e2e/\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n?? runbooks/.supervisor-children/\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GC0001.md:2:task_id: GC0001\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:2:task_id: G0004\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:10:design_authoring_batch: GB0002\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:2:task_id: G0005\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0001.md:2:task_id: G0001\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GB0003.md:2:task_id: GB0003\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GB0002.md:2:task_id: GB0002\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GB0001.md:2:task_id: GB0001\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GD0001.md:2:task_id: GD0001\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0002.md:2:task_id: G0002\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0003.md:2:task_id: G0003\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0003.md:10:d